_insider_buying":false,"_score_insider_buying":28.6,"pf":[],"description_full":"Coherent Corp. develops, manufactures, and markets lasers, transceivers, other optical and optoelectronic devices, modules, and systems worldwide. Its products include critical components consisting of detectors, passive optics, thermal solutions, and PICS; silicon photonics and other advanced optical technologies; and coherent transmission components, transport products, optical amplifiers, passive optical components, optical line systems, and multi-rail platform. The company's Datacenter and Communications segment offers transceivers, co-packaged optics, and optical circuit switches, as well as other systems, such as subsystems, modules, and semiconductor devices for datacenter and communications applications; and VCSELS, EELS, pump lasers, and other components, optics, and ICs for datacenter and communication applications. Its Industrial segment offers excimer lasers, solid-state lasers, and CO2 lasers; laser systems for various industrial applications, including semiconductor capital equipment, display manufacturing, precision manufacturing, and scientific research; and laser systems and subsystems comprising high-power lasers for materials processing. This segment also provides engineered materials, laser optics, thermoelectric components, and advanced ceramic and metal-matrix composite materials and products. It markets its products and services through a direct sales force, representatives, and distributors. The company was formerly known as II-VI Incorporated and changed its name to Coherent Corp. in September 2022. Coherent Corp. was incorporated in 1971 and is headquartered in Saxonburg, Pennsylvania.","ceo_bio":"Mr. James Robert Anderson | CEO, President & Employee Director | Age 53 | Compensation: $4.6M (FY2026)","culture_narrative":"Employs approximately 51K people. Revenue per employee of $138K ranks in the bottom quartile among Technology peers, with revenue growing 19%/yr across its filed history. Stock-based compensation of $4K per employee reflects an ownership culture. CEO compensation is 33\u00d7 revenue per employee (elevated relative to workforce productivity). Governance score flags elevated compensation governance risk (7/10).","financial_summary":["Coherent Corp. is a large-cap technology business with a $36.9B market cap on $7.1B of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at +11% over the past three years and +24% annually across the full decade, a respectable pace for a business of this size.","Returns on capital run at 2% against a 13% cost of capital, which means the business is destroying value with every dollar it reinvests.","The company is burning through $1.0B of cash, and without positive owner earnings any valuation rests on hope rather than evidence.","On the balance sheet, leverage is comfortably conservative at 0.8\u00d7 net debt/EBITDA, and interest coverage runs at 5.5\u00d7.","Net dilution runs at 5.4% annually, transferring value from owners to stock-based comp, and insiders hold 4.4% of the shares."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Price sits 893% above estimated fair value \u2014 no margin of safety left, and the cushion against estimate error has been bid away (confirmed by 1 other valuation measure)","sev":"red","cat":"valuation","magnitude":8.929274796830072},{"text":"Fragmented industry with below-average profit capture \u2014 no moat to protect margins","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Volatile returns on capital suggest the moat is narrower than a snapshot ROIC implies","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Above-average short interest at 5.1% of float","sev":"amber","cat":"sentiment"},{"text":"Insiders are net sellers (71% sell ratio, net $2.4M) \u2014 the people closest to the business are reducing their personal stake","sev":"amber","cat":"insider"},{"text":"Technology sector lagging the market significantly, underperforming by 8% over 3 months","sev":"amber","cat":"sector"},{"text":"Techn